  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find the values of $x$ for which\n$$(x+3)(x+4)<(3x+2)(x+6).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x<-\\dfrac{13}{2}$ or $x>0$.\n\nExpand and collect terms to obtain $x(2x+13)>0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+3)(x+4)&<(3x+2)(x+6)\\\\x^2+7x+12&<3x^2+20x+12\\\\2x^2+13x&>0\\\\x(2x+13)&>0.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth factors must be positive or both negative.\n\nIf both are positive, $x>0$ and $x>-\\dfrac{13}{2}$, so $x>0$.\n\nIf both are negative, $x<0$ and $x<-\\dfrac{13}{2}$, so $x<-\\dfrac{13}{2}$.\n\nTherefore, $x<-\\dfrac{13}{2}$ or $x>0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
